    <mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="Student debt shock"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        Student debt shock
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What happened? </strong>Nine universities have launched judicial measures against the UK government after around <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cnv884qveyqo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">22,000 students in England were told to repay maintenance loans</a> and childcare grants that had already been approved. Universities say the decision was abrupt, unfair, and damaging. Many affected students are close to finishing their three-year courses and were shocked to receive letters demanding repayment on an accelerated basis.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Background:</strong> Although students had originally been approved for maintenance loans, tuition support, and, in some cases, childcare grants, officials later ruled that the courses they enrolled for counted as distance learning. Under existing funding rules, that meant the courses were never actually eligible for that support. The government argues that universities either misunderstood the regulations or abused the system.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Comments from the universities: </strong>Universities said the government’s decision was abrupt, given minimal notice, and had caused serious financial distress for students. They argued they had acted in good faith when these courses were approved for funding and strongly rejected the claim that in-person, timetabled weekend teaching should count as distance learning. They said that it also disproportionately harms students from underrepresented and lower-income backgrounds.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" css-class="border-line" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
